      "solution": "n,c = list(map(int,input().split()))\nd = [0]*(c+1)\nnames = input().split()\nfor i in range(n):\n    a = list(map(int,input().split()))\n    t = 0\n    for j in range(c):\n        d[j]+=(a[j]-(a[j]%10))/10\n        t+=(a[j]%10)/10\n    d[-1]+=t\nm = 0\nfor i in range(c+1):\n    if d[i]>d[m]:\n        m = i\ntotal = 0\nfor i in range(c+1):\n    if d[i]==d[m]:\n        total+=1\nif total!=1 or m==c:\n    print(\"Revote\")\nelse:\n    print(names[m])",
      "statement": "In the Congregation Of Democratic Exoplanets (or CODE for short), there is a voting system to elect a chancellor and to make sure there is no fraud. Each planet elects {{10}} representatives to represent the planet wanting each candidate. \n\n[[support_percentage]], the percentage of the planet's population which supports a candidate, determines how many representatives vote for that candidate, using the following formula:\n\n[[support_percentage]] / 10, rounded down\n\nAny representatives that are not assigned to a candidate vote on {{Revote}} instead.\n\nAfter all the votes are cast by the representatives, the candidate with the most votes win, regardless of whether they have a majority. If multiple people have the most votes are the {{Revote}} section has the most votes, then the votes are recast.\n\nYour job is to create a system that will determine the chancellor after the votes are cast.",
