    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">In the Congregation Of Democratic Exoplanets (or CODE for short), there is a voting system to elect a chancellor and to make sure there is no fraud. Each planet elects <const>10</const> representatives to represent the planet wanting each candidate. <br><br><var>support_percentage</var>, the percentage of the planet's population which supports a candidate, determines how many representatives vote for that candidate, using the following formula:<br><br><var>support_percentage</var> / 10, rounded down<br><br>Any representatives that are not assigned to a candidate vote on <const>Revote</const> instead.<br><br>After all the votes are cast by the representatives, the candidate with the most votes win, regardless of whether they have a majority. If multiple people have the most votes are the <const>Revote</const> section has the most votes, then the votes are recast.<br><br>Your job is to create a system that will determine the chancellor after the votes are cast.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> Two space-separated integers: <var>n</var> and <var>c</var>, representing the number of planets and the number of candidates available to vote for.<br><strong>Line 2:</strong> <var>c</var> space-separated strings, representing the names of the candidates available to vote for.<br><strong>Next <var>n</var> lines:</strong> <var>c</var> space-separated integers that represent <var>support_percentage</var>, the percentage of the population of that planet that supports the candidate at that index.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\">The name representing the new chancellor, or <const>Revote</const> if no chancellor was decided on.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">1 &le; <var>n</var> &le; 200<br>2 &le; <var>c</var> &le; 200<br>1 &le; each candidate's name &le; 20<br>Each candidate's name does not contain any spaces.<br>All candidates' names are unique.<br>0 &le; <var>support_percentage</var> &le; 100<br>sum of <var>support_percentage</var> for a planet = 100</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">1 3\nMoose John Bob\n55 35 10</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">Moose</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
